version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  SNYK-JS-UNDICI-17372658:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          Vulnerable undici version pinned by npm's bundled node-gyp
          dependency (node-gyp@12.x and 13.0.0 all declare undici@^6.25.0).
          Tested npm 11.13.0 / 11.14.0 / 11.16.0 / 11.17.0 — all resolve to
          a vulnerable undici version. Build-time tool only (node-gyp
          compiles native modules during install), not present in the
          running application's request path. No fix available until
          node-gyp bumps its undici dependency.
        expires: '2026-08-20T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-UNDICI-17372754:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          Same root cause as SNYK-JS-UNDICI-17372658 — vulnerable undici
          pinned via npm's bundled node-gyp dependency, build-time only,
          no fix currently available upstream.
        expires: '2026-08-20T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-UNDICI-17372758:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          Same root cause as SNYK-JS-UNDICI-17372658 — vulnerable undici
          pinned via npm's bundled node-gyp dependency, build-time only,
          no fix currently available upstream.
        expires: '2026-08-20T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-BRACEEXPANSION-18313044:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          brace-expansion resolved transitively via npm's bundled
          minimatch (npm@11.18.0 > minimatch@10.2.5 > brace-expansion@5.0.7).
          Build/CLI tooling only — not present in the application runtime
          path (cica-web app scan clean). Fixed in brace-expansion 5.0.8,
          but npm@11.18.0 bundles 5.0.7 and the version isn't independently
          controllable without patching npm's tree. Recheck when npm bumps
          its bundled brace-expansion.
        expires: '2026-08-20T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-DEBIAN13-ATTR-17678182:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          libattr1, introduced by the base image
          node:24.18.1-trixie-slim via coreutils/adduser — a base-OS
          package, not an application dependency. No fix published for
          Debian 13 (trixie); base-image upgrade recommendations do not
          resolve it. Accepted pending upstream Debian patch or a base-image
          migration. Recheck on base-image bump.
        expires: '2026-08-20T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-DEBIAN13-ACL-17677866:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          libacl1, introduced by the base image
          node:24.18.1-trixie-slim via coreutils/sed/adduser/dpkg — a
          base-OS package, not an application dependency. No fix published
          for Debian 13 (trixie); base-image upgrade recommendations do not
          resolve it. Accepted pending upstream Debian patch or a base-image
          migration. Recheck on base-image bump.
        expires: '2026-08-20T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-NANOID-18506894:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          Both nanoid() call sites (CSP nonce in app.js, request-id fallback in the logger) call with no size argument on the secure export.
          The vulnerable functions (customAlphabet/customRandom and the
          nanoid/non-secure module) are never imported, and no user input
          reaches the size parameter, so the infinite-loop DoS is
          unreachable. Fix available in nanoid@5.1.16.
        expires: '2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-NANOID-18506897:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          Same root cause as SNYK-JS-NANOID-18506894 — no-arg nanoid() on the secure export, vulnerable paths not imported, DoS unreachable.
        expires: '2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-UPSTREAM-NODE-18507940:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          node-tar hardlink directory-traversal (CVE-2026-26960) bundled in
          the node:24.18.1-trixie-slim base image. Exploitable only by
          extracting an attacker-controlled tar archive; node-tar is present
          as a build-time/npm-install dependency, not invoked by the running
          cica-web application, which does not extract untrusted archives at
          runtime. Not bound to the network stack (requires local
          read/write/execute). Fixed upstream in Node 26.5.0. Recheck on
          base-image upgrade.
        expires: '2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-BRACEEXPANSION-18512280:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          brace-expansion resolved transitively via npm's bundled
          minimatch (npm@11.18.0 > minimatch@10.2.5 > brace-expansion@5.0.7),
          same dependency chain as SNYK-JS-BRACEEXPANSION-18313044.
          Build/CLI tooling only — not present in the application runtime
          path (cica-web app scan clean). No direct upgrade/patch available;
          fixed upstream in 1.1.18, 2.1.4, 3.0.6, 5.0.9, but npm@11.18.0
          bundles 5.0.7 and the version isn't independently controllable
          without patching npm's tree. Recheck when npm bumps its bundled
          brace-expansion.
        expires: '2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z'